\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"b715838e3577d4fe5faa0037caf1476927cfe01086eba30726b434b22a0760f7","event_uuid":"82da1646-8168-44d7-8076-42411f28cd1b","position":{"commit_sha":"d3b1333f988195bcabd2f746912dc4bf2053933b","position":"1789022889270758001-82da1646-8168-44d7-8076-42411f28cd1b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d12d76acd5c00c017e6751dc19a49aad9b1c6edadb5aa85c632803d197edf335","event_uuid":"1a1c0ca0-601c-4985-8cfa-d88b05f8da7f","position":{"commit_sha":"81a639aaf11a3d95f882d9842e4e6b676b4f4303","position":"1789025894985139702-1a1c0ca0-601c-4985-8cfa-d88b05f8da7f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Progress note: first execution of the independent proof harness reached throwaway repo initialization and ticket creation, then failed in the harness parser because rebar emitted expected warnings before the JSON output. This is not a product divergence signal; I updated the artifact to parse the final JSON line and am rerunning the same proof.","timestamp":1789021506342506001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Progress note: second proof run passed JSON parsing and reached the first compact-all, then the harness suppressed the compact-all failure output by using check=True before printing stdout. I updated the harness to print stdout/stderr before raising so the next run exposes the compact-all failure cause; still no product divergence evidence yet.","timestamp":1789021538779370001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Progress note: third proof run exposed a config-boundary issue in the proof setup, not a product divergence: compact.threshold=0 is rejected by typed config (must be >= 1). I changed the first backfill compaction to use the same high threshold (9999); because the ticket has no snapshot yet, compact-all backfill should create the first snapshot while keeping the recurrence arm count-ineligible for later alpha checks.","timestamp":1789021614200756001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RCA / proof result: plan review passed and I ran the independent two-clone proof under the session artifact redstart-proof-repo. The proof exercised compact-all's snapshot_alpha path: base backfill selected 1 ticket; clone A alpha-selected and compacted after four A-tail comments; clone B alpha-selected and compacted after two B-tail comments; both clones then merged the combined tickets branch and rebar fsck reported 'no issues found' in both clones. The final normalized compiled states were equal, but the merged state had after_comments_have_a_tail=false, after_comments_have_b_tail=true, after_comment_count=10, and the script exited 2 with ANOMALY merged state lost a divergent tail. Interpretation: the later B snapshot superseded the A snapshot without containing A's tail, so equality after merge is a converged-loss state, not a safe reconvergence. This confirms an ADR 0118 safety anomaly; hammerkop must NOT enable snapshot_alpha yet.","timestamp":1789022103452107001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Calibration evidence (read-only live tracker): active_tickets_with_foldable_or_snapshot=9316; tickets_with_snapshots=9315; pending_source_bytes_total=40,201,566; active_snapshot_bytes_total=122,281,708; pending bytes p50/p90/p99=0/12,932/40,976; snapshot bytes p50/p90/p99=4,947/35,489/84,972; pending/snapshot ratio p50/p90/p99=0/0.946/3.452. Alpha candidates: 0.25 selects 3439 tickets (37,803,318 pending bytes / 47,343,786 snapshot bytes); 0.5 selects 2880 (31,600,458 / 30,295,496); 1.0 selects 636 (13,888,003 / 7,341,662); 2.0 selects 226 (7,034,124 / 2,011,541). If/when the concurrency anomaly is fixed, alpha=1.0 remains the recommended starting point, but it is gated off until then.","timestamp":1789022126288762001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Scope-freeze handoff: I started and claimed this evidence-only ADR 0118 proof. Plan review passed. Artifacts live under /Users/joeoakhart/.copilot/session-state/d4d8a7bd-065c-430f-a674-aa966d8e5f8e/files/: redstart-proof.py, redstart-calibration.py, and redstart-proof-repo. The proof is not green: with snapshot_alpha enabled only in the throwaway repo, clone A and B each created divergent byte-alpha snapshots via compact-all; after merge both clones converged and fsck passed, but clone A's tail was absent from final compiled state while B's tail remained. I recorded calibration data and updated plush-excessive-willet as the existing follow-up. Per operator gate, equitable-upper-hammerkop must not enable snapshot_alpha until the concurrent-SNAPSHOT merge-safety issue is fixed. Returning this ticket to open for the next session rather than leaving my claim active.","timestamp":1789022714345415001}],"created_at":1788911818147171001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"08659ed5-48b1-4215-87b7-a5212c60ab84","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"da70-18a5-898d-47ea"}],"description":"Prove the ADR 0118 safety gate before this repository enables `compact.snapshot_alpha`. This ticket is evidence-only: it runs an independent two-clone proof and records the commands/results on the ticket; it does not modify repository code or `rebar.toml`.\n\n## Scope\n- Use an independent throwaway Git repository and clone pair under `/Users/joeoakhart/.copilot/session-state/d4d8a7bd-065c-430f-a674-aa966d8e5f8e/files/redstart-proof-repo`, never the live `.tickets-tracker` store.\n- Configure `compact.snapshot_alpha` only inside the throwaway clones.\n- Create divergent adaptive fold points in two clones, merge/fetch the ticket history, replay compiled ticket state, and run fsck/rebuild checks.\n- Measure this repository's live ticket-size distribution read-only and recommend an alpha with storage/replay tradeoffs.\n- Do not enable `compact.snapshot_alpha` for this repository; that is reserved for `equitable-upper-hammerkop` and is gated on this proof having zero divergence.\n\n## Proof command\nRun the artifact script:\n\n`env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python /Users/joeoakhart/.copilot/session-state/d4d8a7bd-065c-430f-a674-aa966d8e5f8e/files/redstart-proof.py`\n\nThe script executes this concrete proof sequence:\n1. Create a throwaway bare Git remote and clone `clone-a`.\n2. Seed a minimal project with `rebar.toml` containing `[compact] snapshot_alpha = 0.05`, `threshold = 9999`, `COMPACTION_HORIZON_NS = 0`, and normal sync to `origin`.\n3. Run `rebar init`, create one task, add large base comments with sync disabled, and run `REBAR_COMPACT_THRESHOLD=9999 REBAR_COMPACT_SNAPSHOT_ALPHA=0.05 rebar compact-all --limit=1` to create the first snapshot through the same sweep selection path that owns `snapshot_alpha`; the backfill arm selects because no snapshot exists even though count is below the high threshold.\n4. Clone `clone-b` from the same remote and materialize the same ticket store.\n5. In clone A add four large A-tail comments with sync disabled and run `REBAR_COMPACT_THRESHOLD=9999 REBAR_COMPACT_SNAPSHOT_ALPHA=0.05 rebar compact-all --limit=1`; because the foldable count is below 9999 and a snapshot already exists, only the byte alpha arm can select the ticket and create the A fold point.\n6. In clone B add two larger B-tail comments with sync disabled and run the same high-threshold `compact-all --limit=1`, creating a different B fold point through the byte alpha arm.\n7. Publish A, merge A into B, publish B, merge the combined `origin/tickets` branch back to A, run `rebar fsck` in both clones, and compare normalized `rebar show` output. The script uses `subprocess.run(..., check=True)` for every command, so any nonzero or finding-emitting `rebar fsck` makes the proof fail before state equality is accepted.\n8. Fail nonzero if any command fails, either `rebar fsck` fails, final compiled states differ, or either divergent tail is absent from the merged state.\n\n## Calibration command\nRun the read-only live-store measurement artifact:\n\n`env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python /Users/joeoakhart/.copilot/session-state/d4d8a7bd-065c-430f-a674-aa966d8e5f8e/files/redstart-calibration.py`\n\nThe calibration script walks `/Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.tickets-tracker`, measures active SNAPSHOT bytes and active non-snapshot source bytes per ticket, reports percentiles, and compares alpha candidates 0.25, 0.5, 1.0, and 2.0 by estimated future replay-tail bytes and retained snapshot amplification.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Independent two-clone reconvergence proof is run in a non-live throwaway repository and the exact commands/results are recorded in ticket comments.\n- [ ] Divergent adaptive fold points converge after fetch/merge/replay/fsck without data loss or state divergence.\n- [ ] Calibration evidence records this repository's ticket-size distribution and recommends an alpha with storage and replay-cost tradeoffs.\n- [ ] `compact.snapshot_alpha` remains absent from this repository's `rebar.toml` in this ticket, proven with `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -c \"from pathlib import Path; raise SystemExit('snapshot_alpha present' if 'snapshot_alpha' in Path('rebar.toml').read_text() else 0)\"`.\n- [ ] No repository files are changed by this evidence-only proof, including no tracked or untracked changes.\n\n## Verification\n- [ ] Run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python /Users/joeoakhart/.copilot/session-state/d4d8a7bd-065c-430f-a674-aa966d8e5f8e/files/redstart-proof.py`.\n- [ ] Run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python /Users/joeoakhart/.copilot/session-state/d4d8a7bd-065c-430f-a674-aa966d8e5f8e/files/redstart-calibration.py` and record its output on the ticket.\n- [ ] Run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -c \"from pathlib import Path; raise SystemExit('snapshot_alpha present' if 'snapshot_alpha' in Path('rebar.toml').read_text() else 0)\"`.\n- [ ] Run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" git diff --exit-code` and `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" git status --porcelain` to confirm no tracked or untracked repository file changes.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"none","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","da70-18a5-898d-47ea"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"Evidence-only proof recorded on the ticket; independent throwaway repositories live under the session artifact directory and no repository files are changed.","parent_id":"","parent_status_uuid":"93dcfd37-bbb0-4288-8080-6328493f9ea3","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"f670-8d14-15e7-4a04","ticket_type":"task","title":"Prove snapshot_alpha reconvergence and calibrate","verify_commands":[{"command":"ticket comments include the proof transcript and zero-divergence result","dd_id":"AC1","dd_text":"independent proof commands recorded"},{"command":"git diff --exit-code","dd_id":"AC2","dd_text":"repository unchanged"}]},"source_event_uuids":["928275b8-4d31-40fe-80b6-e535c7e18c34","08659ed5-48b1-4215-87b7-a5212c60ab84","1c603e0d-fe3c-4bd2-8cb7-f66b1af04d42","68bf86ee-da66-4389-8635-b09c4f313c22","22e1c118-59c6-4913-8d22-aeaea5dddb9b","80c93bb0-5aca-4b47-8acf-9faeb5f6dfac","b65faf0b-137a-4442-8bff-49ad2ac090ab","e9ace748-7594-4d40-a946-1310b9127ee7","6b54fb15-cfc8-4570-a527-e920f6584809","52faa3e1-cf5e-46a4-930b-b8d4d8f3cd83","ac7dfd76-d4a9-4f3c-8ea7-861689771a03","91d3f37c-ed33-4626-9ac3-c52f061b4546","08e224c6-d869-4e29-a4f0-9610ba50fef4","660a69c1-4df2-4684-ba74-a7f0b3f43a76","4471733a-5590-4e64-8ecc-e41784e17491","c51a9894-82b5-45f1-844e-2e7d302398a1","8d6d7870-a9af-449f-91c1-4cb7775a84e8","c0823165-57a6-4807-9dcd-3647a581ac0b","83a36c18-11ed-4688-8856-4e5f1b1778c0","e80e76bf-69a7-4b91-a270-166febac7fd2","93dcfd37-bbb0-4288-8080-6328493f9ea3","82da1646-8168-44d7-8076-42411f28cd1b","1a1c0ca0-601c-4985-8cfa-d88b05f8da7f"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1789028948639409001,"uuid":"3cd655aa-171f-46c7-81fe-ef26853b483c"}